NAME: an if-else taking its then branch
DESCRIPTION: x = 0: (JZ x) holds, the then branch writes 1 into r and jumps over the else branch; see behtests/if_else_then.beh
SRC:
(let (x 0)
  (let (r 0)
    (seq
      (if (JZ x) (MOV 1 r) (MOV 2 r))
      (JMP 0)
      (DAT (store x) (store r)))))
EXPECTED:
;redcode-94b

  JMN.A  $_IFM5 , $_LET1 
  MOV.AB #1     , $_LET2 
  JMP    $_IFF5 , #0     
_IFM5 
  MOV.AB #2     , $_LET2 
_IFF5 
  JMP    #0     , #0     
_LET1 
_LET2 
  DAT    #0     , #0     
  DAT    $0     , $0     